The fifth programming environment. A sentence ("Show Q5 only when Q3 = Yes
and Q4 > 2", "screen out when Q1 < 18", "add a numeric question 'Age?'
after Q1", "what depends on Q3?") becomes a PROPOSED CHANGE card — the
summary in the Logic panel's words, the condition three ways (canonical
text, sentence, structured tree), every change it will make, and the
errors that block it — with [Review Logic] [Cancel] [Apply]. Nothing is
written until Apply, and Apply is one labelled, undoable store.update.

One engine, no second logic system:
- packages/engine/src/logicProposal.ts: a closed, typed ProposalChange
  vocabulary (set_display_logic, add_skip_rule, add_display_rule,
  set_required, add_question, rename_variable), validateProposal (self
  reads, reads of later questions, backward skips, missing targets, taken
  names, duplicate ids), describeChange (conditionSummary's words) and
  applyLogicProposal — all-or-nothing, in place, through addQuestion and
  renameVariable. 7 tests, mutation-checked.
- apps/studio/lib/intelligent/: Intent (provider-independent), the
  deterministic grammar (display / hide / skip / terminate / required /
  add question / rename / find / explain, with "unless" and everyday
  operator spellings normalised, multi-word operands quoted), the planner
  (resolves codes, variables, question text, page/block titles and
  numbers; parses conditions with parseLogicExpression — the expression
  editor's parser; builds changes; validates), a bounded survey context
  serializer for the model, and coerceIntent as the gate on what a model
  may say. 13 tests, mutation-checked.
- POST /api/ai/logic (completeJson; key from env only; same gate and
  metering as rephrase) returns an intent, never a change; the fake
  provider answers with none so every proposal in tests is the grammar's.
- components/intelligent/IntelligentView.tsx: the renderer — prompt,
  examples ("How do you want to program your research?"), cards, review
  tree, read-only answers as selectable chips, the Architect inspector on
  the proposal's target, conversation kept per survey across mode
  switches. Shared selection: Apply selects the target and Grid opens on
  it.
- MODES.intelligent.available = true; Studio.tsx renders it for the
  questions tab; foundation tests updated (all five modes built).
- scripts/intelligent-mode-test.mjs: 33 checks, against both no provider
  (501 → "grammar only") and AI_API_URL=fake: ("grammar + model").

